        <body>
            <div xml:id="d54">

                <pb facs="0149" n="143" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg143"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward to Mr. McCook.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1867-10-05"><hi rendition="#italic">October 5,
                        1867</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">McCook</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">etc.:</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your dispatch of the 5th of August, No. 31. The President is gratified with
                    the information that His Majesty the King of the Sandwich Islands approves of
                    the reciprocity treaty, and that he took measures to call an extraordinary <pb
                        facs="0150" n="144" xml:id="pg144"/> session of the legislature for the
                    purpose of a formal ratification. Since the receipt of your dispatch we have
                    received a report by the telegraph from San Francisco that the treaty has been
                    finally and fully ratified by the Hawaiian Government.</p>
                <p>I refrain altogether from treating upon the subject of the irritation which has
                    been manifested at Honolulu in connection with the visit of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lackawanna</hi> at that port. No conceivable good could
                    result from engaging in diplomatic debate upon that subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William H.
                    Seward</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
